Take element addresses of std::vector with data() in usort. The sorts
pass &v[0] and &v[v.size()] (or &v[nelem]) as ranges and MPI buffers.
Indexing one past the end, or element 0 of an empty vector, is out of
bounds, and _GLIBCXX_ASSERTIONS aborts on it: every sort through
SpParHelper::KeyValuePSort aborted in Indexing_Test and SpAsgn_Test. Use
v.data() + i, the same address without indexing.

